From e330dee392e6caeb1ff0c735a1d054c30568e864 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozark <ozark@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:13:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Touchscreen support for plugins: keyboard, dialog fit, input
 styles

- TouchInput (installed on the application): tapping any editable text box,
  including plugins' QLineEdits and spin boxes, opens the on-screen
  keyboard, titled from the box's form label and on the numbers layer for
  numeric fields. Plain QDialogs (plugins') are sized to their contents
  and centred with a margin, instead of Qt's default of at most 2/3 of the
  screen, which clipped them and pushed tall ones against the top.
- TextEntry::edit() opens the keyboard for any caller; Dialog::set_area()
  lets a dialog owned by a plugin's dialog lay itself out over the main
  window. Closing a Dash dialog activates the window it was opened over,
  not always the main window (which hid a plugin's dialog behind it).
- Spin boxes and drop-downs are styled like text boxes: unstyled, they
  took the palette's base colour, the theme accent (black on black).
- Keyboard: the last symbols row no longer overlaps backspace.
